From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:29:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(mcp): add the aicd_report handler through the
 barrier

ReportHandler is the handler of aicd_report between S2's pipeline and
ori_memory::barrier::submit_report. It holds the role table (coder:
closing and blocked; documentation: closing, drift audit and blocked; qa:
QA run and blocked; operations: blocked), the two field lists of API_SPEC
section 3 in template order, and refuses qa_run and drift_audit as not
available until a template names their fields.

Every check comes before an identifier is drawn or a byte written: the
ticket, the kind, the role, the content walked in template order (a
missing or blank field before an extra key), and that the ticket is filed
in this product, which S2's check 7 leaves open for every role but the
coder. It then files one NewReportField per field with the raw text
unchanged, maps every barrier error to a fixed unavailable, and answers
with the record id and the fields the cap cut, named in template order.
It appends no event of its own.

